# Python & Backend
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
# Written by `scripts/bootstrap_host.sh` via `poetry config --local
# virtualenvs.in-project true`, which is what puts the environment at
# `backend/.venv` where every no-Poetry fallback in this repository looks for
# it. Machine-local, exactly like `.venv/` itself -- and untracked on purpose,
# because `19_verify_repository_state.sh` requires a clean tree and a bootstrap
# that leaves a new file behind would fail the phase it enables.
backend/poetry.toml
.env
# Every `.env` variant, not just the bare name. `backend/.env.vault-backup` was
# tracked and carried a live provider key into history, which GitHub's push
# protection caught and the W0.1 credential migration did not: a backup taken
# *before* that migration kept the plaintext it was meant to remove. A prefix
# match is the point -- the next variant will not be called `.env` either.
.env.*
!.env.example
# Kept although nothing in the repository creates this any more: it held Vault
unseal material, and an ignore rule guarding against committing a secret costs
nothing to leave in place for anyone who turns PLATFORM_VAULT_ENABLED back on.
.vault-local/

# Generated validation and test output
.manual_llm/
.runtime/
.gate-receipts/
artifacts/
frontend/test-results/
frontend/playwright-report/
backend_results.txt
docker_compose_logs.txt
# Running a service from the repository root (uvicorn, the discovery worker)
# redirects here, so without this every dev session shows a dirty tree.
#
# `backend.log` and `worker.log` were committed once and stayed committed; a
# tracked file ignores its own ignore rule, so the pattern only prevents the
# *next* one. Already-tracked evidence logs under `docs/evidence/` are
# unaffected by this for the same reason, which is what keeps them.
*.log
# Same story: `backend/validation_output_new.txt` was a redirected PowerShell
# traceback that got committed. Redirect targets are named after the run, not
# after a convention, so match the stem rather than one exact name.
validation_output*.txt
playwright_results.txt
linux_kit_validation/

