# Claude Code local state
.claude/settings.local.json

# Agent worktrees. These are real git repositories checked out inside the
# working tree, so `git add -A` stages them as gitlinks and prints seventeen
# "adding embedded git repository" warnings -- and would commit a submodule
# pointer to a clone nobody else has. Ignoring them costs nothing: a worktree
# is a view of this repository's own history, so anything worth keeping is
# already reachable from a branch.
.claude/worktrees/

# Linux-only developer helper, deliberately not committed.
#
# `start_manual_mode.sh` brings the platform up with every reasoning turn
# answered by a human (`PLATFORM_AI_PROVIDER_ORDER=MANUAL`). It is a convenience
# wrapper around checks and scripts that are all in the repository already, and
# it is Linux-only -- it calls `scripts/linux/*` and `scripts/infra.sh`, so it
# is no use to anyone on the Windows host path.
#
# It is also refused by this network's egress inspection: pushes carrying it
# return 403 from the proxy while the identical push without it succeeds,
# isolated 2026-08-28 by pushing each file on its own branch. Presumably the
# block of `PLATFORM_AI_*=` assignments reads as credential configuration; there
# is no secret in the file, which reads variable *names* and reports whether
# they are set.
#
# What it does is written out step by step in
# `.claude/skills/testmanual/SKILL.md`, so nothing is lost by its absence -- the
# script is a shortcut, not the source of truth.
scripts/dev/start_manual_mode.sh

# JUnit reports written by `.github/workflows/checks.yml`. They are an artifact
# of a run, uploaded from CI and read by scripts/ci/assert_known_failures.py --
# never a committed file, including when the same command is run locally.
backend/junit-backend.xml
frontend/junit-frontend.xml
